    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0713" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9405a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Tiflis</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d743-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-30T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1918,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring your recent telegrams March 10 to 15.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d743-f2"/>
                    The United States is not in a position to support active military operations on
                    Caucasus front. Summary of your reports has been communicated to British
                    Government. Messages to Barton<anchor n="3" xml:id="d743-f3"/> and Red Cross
                    also delivered. Department will advise whether any measures possible to relieve
                    situation among civilian population.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d743-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d743-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Legation in Persia (No. 37).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d743-f2" n="2" xml:id="d743-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram to the Ambassador in Great Britain (No. 7116), Apr. 3,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d743-f3" n="3" xml:id="d743-f3-content">
                <p>The Rev. Dr. James L. Barton, foreign secretary of the
                    American Board of Commissioners for Foreign Missions.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
